ass_rate":0.5797,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5263,"def_epa_per_play":0.2262},{"week":16,"opponent":"LAC","home":true,"pf":17.0,"pa":34.0,"off_snaps":56,"epa_per_play":0.03423,"pass_rate":0.5893,"pass_rate_neutral":0.587,"def_epa_per_play":0.4464},{"week":17,"opponent":"WAS","home":false,"pf":30.0,"pa":23.0,"off_snaps":87,"epa_per_play":0.2128,"pass_rate":0.4943,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5179,"def_epa_per_play":0.1965},{"week":18,"opponent":"NYG","home":false,"pf":17.0,"pa":34.0,"off_snaps":53,"epa_per_play":-0.1297,"pass_rate":0.4528,"pass_rate_neutral":0.3667,"def_epa_per_play":0.1347}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2025,"team":"MIN","distance":0.5019,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Kevin O'Connell"},{"season":2025,"team":"JAX","distance":0.5858,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Liam Coen"},{"season":2024,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.6153,"shared":22,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"LV","distance":0.6387,"shared":22,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.6515,"shared":21,"play_caller":"Mike LaFleur"}],"defense":[{"season":2021,"team":"PHI","distance":0.5003,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Jonathan Gannon"},{"season":2021,"team":"MIN","distance":0.5184,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"CHI","distance":0.5705,"shared":22,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"SF","distance":0.5884,"shared":22,"play_caller":"DeMeco Ryans"},{"season":2023,"team":"SF","distance":0.6081,"shared":22,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Cowboys went 7-9-1 in 2025 and were outscored 511 to 471. The offense carried the team, ranking 5th in EPA per play while the defense finished 32nd in EPA allowed. What set them apart was the 3rd most receivers on the field and the lowest 2-Man rate in the league.","offense":"The Cowboys had one of the most efficient offenses in the league, ranking in the top eight in four of the five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix stayed close to what game situations called for. Their biggest outliers in how they lined up were the 3rd most receivers on the field in the league. Dak Prescott ran the passing game, with George Pickens leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Cowboys had one of the worst defenses in the league, ranking 29th or worse in all five main efficiency measures. Their one bright spot was pressure rate, where they ranked 9th. Jadeveon Clowney led the team with 8.5 sacks, and James Houston added 5.5 while playing only 28% of the snaps, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Schematically, they had the lowest 2-Man rate in the league.","special":"The Cowboys were one of the most aggressive teams on fourth down, going for it on 57% of their short-yardage chances in normal situations. Their kickers made 86% of field goals, which was about average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the defensive line, about 23% of the money on the books.","players":"Dak Prescott played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 4,552 yards. George Pickens was the clear top target with 23% of the looks and 1,429 receiving yards. Javonte Williams handled most of the work in the backfield with 62% of the carries. On defense, Jadeveon Clowney led the team with 8.5 sacks and Donovan Wilson picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"Brian Schottenheimer called the offense, and the defensive play caller for this season is not in the coaching data. Their offense looked most like the 2025 Vikings under Kevin O'Connell and the 2025 Jaguars under Liam Coen. Their defense looked most like the 2021 Eagles under Jonathan Gannon and the 2021 Vikings.","trends":"The offense went from 29th in EPA per play in 2024 to 5th in 2025, a big step forward. The defense moved from 30th in EPA allowed per play in 2024 to 32nd in 2025, about where it was. The biggest change in approach was play-action rate, which went from 17% to 27%.","notes":"Every data source is available for 2025. This season uses the newer formation labels, which group singleback, I formation and empty sets together as under center, so those older formation rates are not shown."}}